// Class: BluetoothTimerTool
// Purpose: A utility class for managing periodic, time-based background tasks 
// (e.g., battery level monitoring pulses, connection watchdog timeouts).

// Function: startTimer(Duration duration, VoidCallback callback)
// Logic: Schedules a recurring task that executes the provided callback at defined intervals.
// 1. Initializes/Resets any existing timer instance to prevent overlapping execution loops.
// 2. Configures a Timer object with the specified [duration].
// 3. Uses a periodic timer mechanism (e.g., Timer.periodic) to invoke the [callback] repeatedly.
// 4. Handles edge cases like preventing timer execution if the application/Bluetooth context is disposed.

// Function: stopTimer()
// Logic: Perfroms an immediate teardown of any active scheduled tasks.
// 1. Checks if a running timer instance exists.
// 2. Calls `.cancel()` on the active Timer object to halt execution and release resources.
// 3. Clears the reference to the timer instance from memory.

// Function: resetTimer()
// Logic: Restarts the interval from zero without allowing for external duration changes.
// 1. Triggers a stop and restart sequence using the previously configured frequency.

// Summary of file: bluetooth_timer_tool.dart
// This utility is critical for maintaining the "heartbeat" of the Bluetooth connection,
// ensuring that the app-side state (like battery level or signal strength) is 
